  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Match List I with List II.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>List-I<br />\t\t\t(Anion)</strong></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>List-II<br />\t\t\t(gas evolved on reaction with dil. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">H</mi><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">SO</mi><mn mathvariant=\"bold\">4</mn></msub></math>)</strong></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(A)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(I)</td>\t\t\t<td>\t\t\t<p>Colourless gas which turns lead acetate paper black.</p>\t\t\t</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(B)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(II)</td>\t\t\t<td>\t\t\t<p>Colourless gas which turns acidified potassium dichromate solution green.</p>\t\t\t</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(C)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(III)</td>\t\t\t<td>Brown fumes which turns acidified KI solution containing starch blue.</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(D)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(IV)</td>\t\t\t<td>Colourless gas evolved with brisk effervescence, which turns lime water milky.</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>",
